  "interpretation": [
    "Admitted tiered RossFast remains route-valid in all 216 E0 characterization cases; the same three high-saturation B cases remain Reference non-convergences while RossFast succeeds at K2.",
    "Aggregate solver-only shared-host screening is resolved in favor of RossFast: about 17.7% lower solver CPU, corresponding to mean Reference/RossFast speedup about 1.216.",
    "The performance advantage is generated by K2: on the 209 paired-valid K2 cases RossFast uses about 78.7% of Reference solver CPU on average. K4 and K8 fallback cases are individually more expensive than Reference.",
    "Fallback remains rare: 212/216 cases finish at K2, two O01 high-saturation cases finish at K4, and two B05 high-saturation cases finish at K8.",
    "The advantage strengthens with saturation in aggregate: roughly 5.2% lower solver CPU at Se=0.65, 19.3% at Se=0.85, and 25.2% at Se=0.98 on paired-valid cases.",
    "At individual-case level the solver is not uniformly faster: 185/213 cases favor RossFast, 20 favor Reference, and 8 are unresolved. All four K4/K8 paired cases favor Reference.",
    "Historical P2E10 direct-state thresholds remain descriptive only; four paired cases exceed one or more of those historical six-material thresholds, two of them only by storage roundoff-scale differences.",
    "Whole-child CPU and wall-clock improvements are smaller (~4.36%) than solver-only improvement because process/setup overhead dilutes the solver gain."
  ],
